Source Analysis: IASME Consortium – Cyber Essentials Certification Process and Assessment Framework
1. Source Overview

This source analysis examines material published by IASME Consortium Ltd, the official delivery partner for the UK Cyber Essentials scheme. The source set includes website guidance, certification process information, the Cyber Essentials Plus Test Specification v3.2 (April 2025), the Cyber Essentials Requirements for IT Infrastructure v3.2 (April 2025), insurance information, assessor requirements, and supply chain assurance guidance.

IASME is a significant source for this project because it provides practical detail on how Cyber Essentials operates in real certification settings. While the National Cyber Security Centre (NCSC) defines the technical baseline of the scheme, IASME explains how applicants engage with certification, how assessors interpret requirements, and how organisations move from self-assessment to verified technical audit. This makes IASME particularly relevant to the proposed Tanasiom Aegis Cyber Essentials readiness toolkit, as the artefact is designed to help SMEs prepare for this real-world process.

