4.2 Cyber Essentials Plus

Cyber Essentials Plus is described by IASME as a technical audit of IT systems and is only available once an organisation has already completed the verified self-assessment stage. Although it is based on the same technical requirements, it involves hands-on testing of systems to confirm that the controls are genuinely in place.

IASME states that this audit covers:

a representative sample of user devices
all internet gateways
all servers with internet-accessible services

This is important because it demonstrates that the scheme moves beyond declared compliance and into practical verification. For this project, that strengthens the case for a readiness toolkit that goes beyond helping applicants fill in answers and instead supports actual implementation.

